{
 "id": "food-versus-all-energy",
 "title": "Dietary energy against all energy, per person",
 "description": "What a person eats, next to what a person uses, in the same units. Dietary intake is the energy a human body actually runs on; everything above it is energy arranged to be burned on that person's behalf. The ratio is about seventeen to one, up from thirteen in 1965 \u2014 and note that the lower line has been rising too.",
 "group": "throughput",
 "sources": [
